 "structural_change": "rt_h (Claude group-B r2/B3 10-14): rt_g routed TT -102.77 / FF -38.32 / DRC 0 with three logic-depth classes, each fixed at the source, cycle-identical (short bench CASE lines byte-identical to rt_g source): (1) out_ready -> u_bo head_d 13 levels: the bfifo next head is a 2:1 of two candidates formed from registered state only, o_r selects; (2) u_hub.core f1_c -> f2_gt 18 / f1_s -> f2_e 13 levels: lane keys (canon/mono/~index, NaN flag) formed in front of the F1 register from the boundary FIFO head and the cursor register, F1->F2 holds only the 53-b threshold compare; (3) relay g_rel en -> od 19 levels: the merge node head/spill pair (parent pop steering all 108 data loads) is a 2-entry pointer FIFO, data written once at wp, od a 2:1 by rp. Children (heap rt_b, lane rt_e) unchanged. Short exact PASS (11 cases), BYP/CLR/REV/FIFO-head mutants FAIL."
